usage: -c [-h] --output OUTPUT --algorithm {baseline,candidate}
          [--candidate-config CANDIDATE_CONFIG]
          [--report-level {summary,full}]
          [--artifact-level {minimal,provenance,audit}]
          [--maximum-post-seconds MAXIMUM_POST_SECONDS] [--defer-3d]
          [--trajectory-cache TRAJECTORY_CACHE] [--config CONFIG]
          [--progress-range START END] [--split {development,validation}]
          input

Run a locked video baseline or candidate experiment

positional arguments:
  input

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT
  --algorithm {baseline,candidate}
  --candidate-config CANDIDATE_CONFIG
  --report-level {summary,full}
  --artifact-level {minimal,provenance,audit}
  --maximum-post-seconds MAXIMUM_POST_SECONDS
  --defer-3d
  --trajectory-cache TRAJECTORY_CACHE
                        Verified real ORB trajectory cache produced by
                        g305-video-freeze-trajectory.
  --config CONFIG
  --progress-range START END
                        Restrict development work to a closed cumulative-
                        motion interval in [0, 1].
  --split {development,validation}
                        Name the immutable non-holdout split containing
                        --progress-range.
